cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the measurement artifacts, please cite the paper."
title: "The Integer Alibi: Localizing Cross-Kernel Divergence in INT8-Quantized LLM Inference"
abstract: >-
  Two GPU kernels implementing the same scaled INT8 GEMM interface are usually
  treated as interchangeable. Holding the checkpoint, prompts, hardware,
  inference engine, decoding and quantization configuration fixed and swapping
  only the INT8 linear kernel, each arm is individually deterministic yet the
  arms agree on no greedy sequence. Because the INT32 dot product is exact and
  order-independent under a verified no-overflow bound, the accumulator is
  excluded as a source, which localizes the divergence to scale application and
  output rounding; a power-of-two scale probe restores bitwise agreement per
  layer and end to end.
